        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>JEHOHANAN</strong> Jehovah-granted, Jeroboam II. (1.) A Korhite, the head of one of the divisions of the temple porters (1 Chronicles 26:3). (2.) One of Jehoshaphat’s “captains” (2 Chronicles 17:15). (3.) The father of Azariah (2 Chronicles 28:12). (4.) The son of Tobiah, an enemy of the Jews (Nehemiah 6:18). (5.) Nehemiah 12:42. (6.) Nehemiah 12:13.",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
